# value_slot_bucket.tkr — the COL-F0a bucket-mark fixture (crumb 0021). `main.tks` `place`s M large
# `big::Big` value slots and, for each, reassigns the slot with `teko::mem::write` to a fresh value,
# reading before and after to confirm the overwrite took. Reassignment marks the old value dead
# (bucket) but frees NOTHING mid-region: every `place` returns a fresh, DISTINCT address (the bump
# only grows) and the physical bytes leave only at the region's bulk drop. Exits 0 only if all M
# reassignments took, the token count equals M, and the M slot addresses are all live and pairwise
# distinct — the signature of zero mid-region reclaim. The compiler never runs the VALUE `set` path
# itself, so this is not fixpoint-exercised. Pinned to the C backend: the VALUE regime emits on the
# C route and the native leg honest-stops.

Feature: value_slot_bucket — a VALUE-slot reassignment marks dead only; zero mid-region reclaim

  Scenario: reassigning_m_value_slots_reclaims_nothing_mid_region_token_equals_m
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
